                <pb facs="0588" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/6–2648: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-06-26T18:00:00+09:00">June 26, 1948—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 26—8:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1160. Embassy transmitting text article III bilateral contained Deptel 923 of
                    June 24, 11 p.m. (received June 26) to Foreign Office in absence important
                    Embassy reservations. It may prove stronger dose, particularly paragraph 3, than
                    Foreign Office feels Government can take, but we will do best secure
                    acceptance.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1160, repeated Shanghai 532.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
